# Empty of rules, deliberately.
#
# /b/:id, /a/:id and /p/:id used to be 200-rewrites onto client-rendered shells
# (book.html etc.) that fetched their content in the browser — which is why a
# crawler saw "Opening the book…" and no book. Those shells are gone: every page
# is now server-rendered by a Pages Function, so the crawler and the reader get
# the same HTML.
#
# The three legacy paths are now handled by functions/b|a|p/[id].js, which 301 to
# the canonical slug URL. They are kept forever — they are in Google's index, in
# every share card ever generated, and bound to the app's universal links via
# .well-known/apple-app-site-association, which iOS only re-evaluates at install.
#
# Redirects that must run BEFORE a Function would match still belong in here.
